sequenceDiagram
    participant US as Userspace loader
    participant LIB as libbpf skeleton
    participant BPF as BPF verifier/maps
    participant LNK as bpf_link<br/>(.struct_ops.link)
    participant TCP as TCP CC subsystem
    participant SK as Application socket

    US->>LIB: open .bpf.o with callbacks + vtable
    LIB->>BPF: BPF_PROG_LOAD each struct_ops callback
    Note over BPF: signatures checked against kernel BTF vtable
    LIB->>BPF: create/update struct_ops map
    Note over BPF: map stores callback pointers
    LIB->>LNK: attach struct_ops link
    LNK->>TCP: register tcp_congestion_ops name
    Note over TCP: algorithm appears in available_congestion_control
    SK->>TCP: setsockopt(TCP_CONGESTION, name)
    TCP->>BPF: invoke selected callbacks on TCP events
    Note over BPF: BPF code is now part of the CC algorithm
    US->>LNK: close/destroy link
    LNK->>TCP: unregister algorithm
    Note over TCP: sockets can no longer select this BPF CC
